  STORIES.push(
    {id:'long-b1-the-community-garden',title:'The Community Garden',level:'B1',tone:'#9AD9C4',emoji:'🌿',minutes:7,pages:[
      {scene:'🏙️',text:'For years, the empty lot behind the apartment blocks collected rubbish. When the council announced that it might sell the land, a few residents proposed turning it into a community garden. The idea sounded pleasant, but nobody was sure who would do the work.',ar:'لسنوات، كانت الأرض الخالية خلف العمارات تتجمع فيها النفايات. وعندما أعلن المجلس أنه قد يبيعها، اقترح بعض السكان تحويلها إلى حديقة مجتمعية. بدت الفكرة جميلة، لكن لم يعرف أحد من سيتولى العمل.'},
      {scene:'🧤',text:'At the first meeting, everyone suggested what the garden should include: benches, flowers, vegetables and a small play area. The discussion went on for an hour, yet no one volunteered to organise the next step. Maya, who had only come to listen, offered to create a simple rota so that each household could contribute a little time.',ar:'في الاجتماع الأول، اقترح الجميع ما ينبغي أن تتضمنه الحديقة: مقاعد وأزهارًا وخضروات ومساحة صغيرة للعب. استمر النقاش ساعة، لكن لم يتطوع أحد لتنظيم الخطوة التالية. عرضت مايا، التي جاءت للاستماع فقط، إعداد جدول مناوبات كي تساهم كل أسرة بوقت قليل.'},
      {scene:'🌱',text:'The rota revealed a problem that the enthusiastic discussion had hidden. Many residents were available at weekends, but almost nobody could water the plants on weekday afternoons. Instead of abandoning the project, the group planted hardy herbs and installed a rainwater barrel. They also agreed to review the arrangement after a month.',ar:'كشف جدول المناوبات مشكلة أخفاها النقاش المتحمس. كان كثير من السكان متاحين في عطلة نهاية الأسبوع، لكن قلّما استطاع أحد سقي النباتات بعد ظهر أيام العمل. وبدل التخلي عن المشروع، زرعت المجموعة أعشابًا تتحمل الظروف وركبت برميلًا لمياه المطر، واتفقوا على مراجعة الترتيب بعد شهر.'},
      {scene:'🤝',text:'By summer, the garden was not quite the picture-perfect space some residents had imagined. One corner remained untidy, and the play area had been postponed. Nevertheless, people who had barely spoken to one another were now sharing tools and exchanging advice. Maya realised that the most important harvest was not the vegetables, but the sense that the space belonged to everyone.',ar:'بحلول الصيف، لم تكن الحديقة مثالية كما تخيلها بعض السكان. بقي ركن غير مرتب وتأجلت مساحة اللعب. ومع ذلك، صار أشخاص بالكاد تحدثوا سابقًا يتبادلون الأدوات والنصائح. أدركت مايا أن أهم حصاد لم يكن الخضروات، بل شعور الجميع بأن المكان ملك لهم.'}
    ],vocab:{rota:{meaning:'a schedule that shares duties among people',ar:'جدول مناوبات',pronunciation:'ROH-tuh',example:'The rota shows who waters the plants each day.'},hardy:{meaning:'able to survive difficult conditions',ar:'قادر على تحمل الظروف الصعبة',pronunciation:'HAR-dee',example:'Hardy plants need less care.'},harvest:{meaning:'the gathering of a crop; also a result of effort',ar:'حصاد؛ ونتيجة الجهد مجازًا',pronunciation:'HAR-vist',example:'The project’s greatest harvest was trust.'}},questions:[
      {q:'What did the first meeting reveal, despite all the ideas?',answers:['People had not yet agreed who would organise the work','Residents disliked the idea of a garden','The council had already sold the land'],correct:0,explain:'Many suggestions were made, but nobody initially took responsibility for the next step.'},
      {q:'Why did the group choose hardy herbs and a rainwater barrel?',answers:['To work around the lack of weekday watering and use available water','Because residents wanted to remove every plant','To make the garden more expensive'],correct:0,explain:'These choices responded practically to the watering problem.',reviewWord:['hardy','able to survive difficult conditions','B1']},
      {q:'What is implied by the phrase “the discussion had hidden” the problem?',answers:['The group’s enthusiasm distracted them from practical details','Someone deliberately lied about the rota','The residents had already solved the problem'],correct:0,explain:'Positive ideas dominated the conversation before practical constraints were considered.'},
      {q:'What is the author’s main point in the final paragraph?',answers:['The garden’s social value became more important than its perfect appearance','The garden succeeded because every original plan was completed','The residents stopped cooperating by summer'],correct:0,explain:'The ending contrasts an imperfect physical space with stronger community relationships.'}
    ]},
    {id:'long-b2-the-four-day-week',title:'The Four-Day Week',level:'B2',tone:'#C5B8FF',emoji:'📅',minutes:8,pages:[
      {scene:'🏢',text:'When a software company announced a six-month trial of a four-day working week, the headline sounded straightforward: the same pay, fewer days, and happier employees. Behind the announcement, however, the leadership team had argued for weeks about what “the same amount of work” would actually mean.',ar:'عندما أعلنت شركة برمجيات تجربة أسبوع عمل من أربعة أيام لمدة ستة أشهر، بدا العنوان واضحًا: الراتب نفسه، أيام أقل، وموظفون أسعد. لكن خلف الإعلان، ناقش فريق الإدارة لأسابيع معنى «الكمية نفسها من العمل».'},
      {scene:'📊',text:'Some managers proposed squeezing five days of meetings into four. Others argued that this would simply compress the same interruptions into a shorter period. The trial therefore began with two rules: meetings needed a clear purpose, and employees could reserve blocks of uninterrupted time for focused tasks.',ar:'اقترح بعض المديرين ضغط اجتماعات خمسة أيام في أربعة. ورأى آخرون أن ذلك سيكدس المقاطعات نفسها في مدة أقصر. لذلك بدأت التجربة بقاعدتين: يجب أن يكون لكل اجتماع هدف واضح، ويمكن للموظفين حجز فترات عمل دون مقاطعة.'},
      {scene:'⚖️',text:'The early results were mixed. Staff satisfaction rose, and fewer people reported exhaustion by Friday. Yet customer response times worsened in one department because its rota had not been redesigned. The company had measured employee well-being carefully but had underestimated the need to maintain coverage for clients.',ar:'كانت النتائج الأولى مختلطة. ارتفع رضا الموظفين وقلّ الإبلاغ عن الإرهاق يوم الجمعة. لكن زمن الرد على العملاء تدهور في قسم لأن جدول المناوبات لم يُعد تصميمه. قاست الشركة رفاه الموظفين بعناية لكنها قللت من أهمية استمرار خدمة العملاء.'},
      {scene:'🔁',text:'Rather than declare the trial either a triumph or a failure, the company changed the rota and repeated the measurement. The second review suggested that fewer working days could be sustainable, but only when the design of the work changed as well. The lesson was less catchy than the original headline, yet more useful: reducing hours does not automatically reduce workload.',ar:'بدل إعلان التجربة نجاحًا أو فشلًا، عدلت الشركة جدول المناوبات وكررت القياس. وأشارت المراجعة الثانية إلى أن تقليل أيام العمل قد يكون مستدامًا، لكن فقط عندما تتغير طريقة تنظيم العمل أيضًا. كانت الخلاصة أقل جاذبية من العنوان، لكنها أكثر فائدة: تقليل الساعات لا يقلل عبء العمل تلقائيًا.'}
    ],vocab:{compress:{meaning:'to fit something into less time or space',ar:'يضغط في وقت أو مساحة أقل',pronunciation:'kum-PRES',example:'Do not compress every meeting into one morning.'},coverage:{meaning:'the provision of service or availability across a period',ar:'تغطية الخدمة واستمرارها',pronunciation:'KUV-er-ij',example:'The rota must maintain customer coverage.'},sustainable:{meaning:'able to continue over time without causing unacceptable problems',ar:'قابل للاستمرار',pronunciation:'suh-STAY-nuh-bul',example:'A sustainable schedule protects both staff and clients.'}},questions:[
      {q:'Why did the company limit the number of meetings?',answers:['To reduce interruptions and protect focused work time','To prevent employees from talking to clients','To make the trial appear more successful'],correct:0,explain:'The company aimed to change how work was organised, not merely squeeze it into fewer days.'},
      {q:'What weakness did the first review expose?',answers:['Customer service coverage had not been planned well enough','Employees refused to take part','The company reduced salaries'],correct:0,explain:'One department’s rota was not redesigned, so response times suffered.'},
      {q:'What is the tone of the final paragraph?',answers:['Cautiously constructive: the idea may work with adjustments','Triumphant and certain that every company should copy it','Sarcastic and dismissive of all experiments'],correct:0,explain:'The writer recognises promise while emphasising conditions and limitations.'},
      {q:'What does the final sentence challenge?',answers:['The assumption that fewer hours automatically mean less work','The idea that customers need responses','The use of any measurements'],correct:0,explain:'The workload itself must be redesigned; shorter time alone does not guarantee less work.'}
    ]},
    {id:'long-c1-the-missing-data',title:'The Missing Data',level:'C1',tone:'#A8D8F0',emoji:'🔬',minutes:9,pages:[
      {scene:'📉',text:'A city report claimed that a new traffic policy had reduced congestion by twelve per cent. The figure quickly appeared in presentations and headlines, where it was treated as evidence that the policy had worked. Few readers noticed that the report’s appendix described several gaps in the underlying data.',ar:'زعم تقرير بلدي أن سياسة مرورية جديدة خفضت الازدحام بنسبة اثني عشر بالمئة. انتشر الرقم سريعًا في العروض والعناوين بوصفه دليلًا على نجاح السياسة. ولم يلاحظ إلا قليلون أن الملحق أشار إلى فجوات في البيانات الأساسية.'},
      {scene:'🧾',text:'The monitoring system had failed intermittently at two of the busiest junctions during the comparison period. Analysts had estimated the missing readings using nearby sensors. That approach was not necessarily unreasonable, but the report did not explain how sensitive the final percentage was to those estimates.',ar:'تعطل نظام الرصد بشكل متقطع عند تقاطعين مزدحمين خلال فترة المقارنة. وقدّر المحللون القراءات المفقودة باستخدام مستشعرات قريبة. لم يكن ذلك غير معقول بالضرورة، لكن التقرير لم يوضح مدى تأثر النسبة النهائية بهذه التقديرات.'},
      {scene:'🧠',text:'An independent researcher repeated the calculation under several plausible assumptions. In one scenario, the reduction remained close to twelve per cent; in another, it fell to four. Neither result proved the policy ineffective. Instead, the range showed that the headline figure conveyed more certainty than the data justified.',ar:'أعاد باحث مستقل الحساب وفق عدة افتراضات معقولة. بقي الانخفاض قريبًا من اثني عشر بالمئة في أحد السيناريوهات، لكنه هبط إلى أربعة في سيناريو آخر. لم يثبت أي من ذلك فشل السياسة؛ بل أظهر النطاق أن الرقم الرئيسي أوحى بيقين أكبر مما تبرره البيانات.'},
      {scene:'📰',text:'The city revised its statement, describing the policy as promising while committing to improve monitoring. Some commentators called the revision an admission of failure. The researcher disagreed: revising a claim in response to uncertainty, they argued, is not retreat from evidence but a basic condition of taking evidence seriously.',ar:'عدلت البلدية بيانها ووصفت السياسة بأنها واعدة مع التعهد بتحسين الرصد. واعتبر بعض المعلقين التعديل اعترافًا بالفشل. لكن الباحث خالفهم: تعديل الادعاء استجابة لعدم اليقين ليس تراجعًا عن الأدلة، بل شرط أساسي لأخذها بجدية.'}
    ],vocab:{intermittently:{meaning:'at irregular intervals, not continuously',ar:'على فترات متقطعة',pronunciation:'in-ter-MIT-unt-lee',example:'The sensor worked intermittently during the storm.'},sensitive:{meaning:'likely to change noticeably when conditions change',ar:'حساس للتغيرات',pronunciation:'SEN-si-tiv',example:'The estimate is sensitive to missing data.'},retreat:{meaning:'a withdrawal from a position or claim',ar:'تراجع عن موقف أو ادعاء',pronunciation:'ri-TREET',example:'Updating a conclusion is not necessarily a retreat.'}},questions:[
      {q:'Why does the writer mention the report’s appendix?',answers:['To show that important limitations were present but easy to overlook','To prove the entire report was fabricated','To suggest that appendices are never useful'],correct:0,explain:'The appendix contained caveats that were overshadowed by the headline figure.'},
      {q:'What does the range from four to twelve per cent demonstrate?',answers:['The result depends meaningfully on assumptions about missing readings','The policy definitely increased congestion','All estimates are equally reliable'],correct:0,explain:'Different plausible assumptions produced materially different estimates.',reviewWord:['sensitive','likely to change noticeably when conditions change','C1']},
      {q:'Which claim does the researcher explicitly avoid making?',answers:['That uncertainty proves the policy was ineffective','That the original figure was perfectly certain','That the monitoring system had no gaps'],correct:0,explain:'The researcher says the uncertainty weakens confidence in the precise figure but does not prove failure.'},
      {q:'What is the author’s attitude toward revising the city’s statement?',answers:['It is responsible when the evidence does not support certainty','It is always a sign of incompetence','It should be avoided to protect public confidence'],correct:0,explain:'The writer presents qualification as a sign of taking evidence seriously.'}
    ]},
    {id:'long-c2-the-language-of-neutrality',title:'The Language of Neutrality',level:'C2',tone:'#D6C6F6',emoji:'🗞️',minutes:10,pages:[
      {scene:'📰',text:'The editorial described its new reporting guidelines as a return to neutrality. Reporters were instructed to avoid “emotive language” and to present both sides of a dispute. At first glance, the policy seemed difficult to oppose: accuracy and fairness are widely accepted journalistic ideals.',ar:'وصف المقال الافتتاحي إرشادات التحرير الجديدة بأنها عودة إلى الحياد. وطُلب من الصحفيين تجنب «اللغة العاطفية» وعرض جانبي النزاع. بدا من الصعب الاعتراض على السياسة ظاهريًا، فالدقة والإنصاف من مبادئ الصحافة المقبولة.'},
      {scene:'⚖️',text:'The difficulty emerged in practice. A report on a proposed factory quoted the company’s economic forecast and a resident’s fear of pollution, then gave each statement equal space. It did not examine the company’s assumptions or explain whether the resident’s concern was supported by environmental measurements. Equal length had been mistaken for equal evidential weight.',ar:'ظهرت الصعوبة في التطبيق. نقل تقرير عن مصنع مقترح توقعات الشركة الاقتصادية ومخاوف أحد السكان من التلوث، ومنح كل تصريح المساحة نفسها. لكنه لم يفحص افتراضات الشركة أو يوضح ما إذا كانت مخاوف الساكن مدعومة بقياسات بيئية. فقد خلط التقرير بين تساوي المساحة وتساوي الوزن الاستدلالي.'},
      {scene:'🔍',text:'Critics argued that neutrality cannot mean withholding relevant context. Yet they also warned against replacing one formula with another: journalists should not decide in advance which side deserves belief. The task is to scrutinise the quality of each claim, disclose uncertainty and distinguish what is known from what remains disputed.',ar:'جادل النقاد بأن الحياد لا يعني حجب السياق ذي الصلة. لكنهم حذروا أيضًا من استبدال قاعدة جامدة بأخرى: فلا ينبغي للصحفيين تقرير مسبقًا أي طرف يستحق التصديق. المطلوب فحص جودة كل ادعاء، وإظهار عدم اليقين، والتمييز بين المعلوم وما لا يزال موضع خلاف.'},
      {scene:'🧭',text:'The debate revealed that neutrality is not simply a tone of voice. A calm sentence can still mislead if it places a well-supported finding beside an unsupported assertion as though the two were equivalent. Fairness, in this account, requires restraint in judgement—but not restraint in examining evidence.',ar:'كشف النقاش أن الحياد ليس مجرد نبرة هادئة. فقد تكون الجملة الهادئة مضللة إذا وضعت نتيجة مدعومة جيدًا بجانب ادعاء غير مدعوم كما لو كانا متكافئين. ووفق هذا التصور، يتطلب الإنصاف ضبط الأحكام، لا الامتناع عن فحص الأدلة.'}
    ],vocab:{scrutinise:{meaning:'to examine something very carefully',ar:'يدقق في',pronunciation:'SKROO-tuh-nyze',example:'Readers should scrutinise the assumptions behind a claim.'},equivalent:{meaning:'equal in value, meaning, or importance',ar:'مكافئ أو مساوٍ',pronunciation:'ih-KWIV-uh-lunt',example:'Equal airtime does not make evidence equivalent.'},restraint:{meaning:'the ability to control an action or judgement',ar:'ضبط النفس أو التريث',pronunciation:'ri-STRAYNT',example:'Good analysis requires restraint in judgement.'}},questions:[
      {q:'What is the central flaw in giving each statement equal space?',answers:['It can imply equal credibility despite unequal supporting evidence','It guarantees that readers will reject the report','It prevents companies from commenting'],correct:0,explain:'The passage distinguishes equal presentation from equal evidential strength.'},
      {q:'Why do the critics reject replacing neutrality with a new formula?',answers:['Because journalists must evaluate evidence rather than decide in advance who is right','Because every claim should be accepted without checking','Because context should never be included'],correct:0,explain:'They warn against pre-judging either side and instead advocate scrutiny of claims.'},
      {q:'What is implied by “a calm sentence can still mislead”?',answers:['A neutral tone does not guarantee a fair or accurate representation','Emotional language is always more accurate','Readers should ignore writing style entirely'],correct:0,explain:'The author separates a calm tone from the fairness of the underlying comparison.'},
      {q:'Which best captures the author’s view of neutrality?',answers:['It requires careful judgement about evidence, not mechanical balance','It means never questioning either side','It is achieved by using equally long quotations'],correct:0,explain:'The conclusion argues for restraint in judgement alongside active examination of evidence.'}
    ]}
  );

